papers.abstract:
We study the nonlinear Kirchhoff equation on the waveguide manifolds $\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{T}^n$: \begin{align*}
  -\left( a+b \int_{\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{T}^n}|\nabla_{x,y}u(x,y)|^2\,dxdy\right) \Delta_{x,y}u+\omega u=|u|^\alpha u, \end{align*} where $a,b>0$, $\omega\in \mathbb{R}$, $\alpha\in(0,2^*)$. We first establish existence of the normalized ground states when $\alpha\in(0,2^*)$.
  To precisely characterize the $y$-dependence of ground states, we apply a scaling argument to handle the integral term $ \int_{\mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{T}^n} |\nabla_{x,y} u(x,y)|^2 dxdy$. To this end, we construct two distinct modified energy functionals, through which we establish the $y$-independence and $y$-dependence of the ground states in two specific regimes: $(i)$ $ d + n \leq 4$ and $\alpha \in (0, \frac{8}{d+n})$; $(ii)$ $d = n = 1$ and $\alpha \in (8, \infty)$.

We prove that the discrete Bilinear Hilbert Transform along the primes,
  \begin{align}
  \mathcal{H}_{\mathbb{P}}(f,g)(x) := \sum_{n \neq 0} \frac{\Lambda(|n|)}{n} f(x-n) g(x+n), \qquad \Lambda(n) := \begin{cases} \log p & \text{ if } n = p^k, \ k \geq 1
  \\ 0 & \text{ otherwise} \end{cases}
  \end{align}
  extends to a bounded operator from $\ell^p \times \ell^q \to \ell^r$ whenever $p,q \in (1,\infty)$ and $\frac{1}{r}=\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{q}$ in the Banach range, $r \geq 1$, and a particular portion of the quasi-Banach range $r \in \left(\frac{2}{3},1\right)$; in the diagonal case, this extends up to the endpoint $(\frac{5}{3},\frac{5}{3},\frac{5}{6})$. After $U^3$-based reductions, the philosophy of the proof becomes similar to that of Krause-Mirek-Tao (on different bilinear operators in discrete harmonic analysis), namely a ``splitting" of the problem into an arithmetic component, handled by analysis within cyclic subgroups, and an analytic component, handled by analysis along arithmetic progressions. For the arithmetic component, we draw upon previous work of most of the authors on Carleson operators along the primes; the main analytic input are estimates for UMD space-valued bilinear singular integrals with modulation invariance, due to Di Plinio-Li-Martikainen-Vuorinen.

We solve the minimizer case of Brezis's Open Problem~2.3 for every fixed $p>2$. For $\varepsilon>0$, let $\mathbf{u}_{\varepsilon}\in W^{1,p}(B_1;\mathbb{R}^2)$ be a global minimizer of the $p$-Ginzburg--Landau energy \[
  \int_{B_1}
  \left(
  \frac{|\nabla\mathbf{u}|^p}{p}
  +\frac{(1-|\mathbf{u}|^2)^2}{4\varepsilon^2}
  \right)\,dx \] with prescribed trace $\mathbf{u}_{\varepsilon}|_{\partial B_1}(x)=x$. We prove that, as $\varepsilon\downarrow0$, $\mathbf{u}_{\varepsilon}(x)\to x/|x|$ at every point $x\in B_1\setminus\{0\}$. The convergence is strong in $W^{1,p}_{\mathrm{loc}}(B_1\setminus\{0\};\mathbb{R}^2)$ and hence uniform on every compact subset of the punctured disk. On each such compact subset, the potential energy tends to zero and the total energy converges to the $p$-Dirichlet energy of the radial map. No symmetry or uniqueness of the minimizers is assumed. The proof combines whole-plane concentration, a strict exterior filling estimate, and quantitative convexity to locate the concentration point and identify the limiting map.

We study the initial value problem associated with the dispersive generalized Benjamin-Ono equation
  \begin{equation*}
  \partial_{t}u-\partial_{x}|D_{x}|^{a}u+u\,\partial_{x}u=0,\quad 1<a<2,
  \end{equation*}
  in weighted Sobolev spaces. First, we show that if the solution belongs to $L^{2}(|x|^{2\alpha}dx)$ at two different times, then it gains regularity, namely $u\in C([-T,T]:H^{a\alpha}(\mathbb{R}))$, for $\alpha<5/2+a$ and suitable initial regularity. Second, we establish the persistence of the solution flow in $H^{s}(\mathbb{R})\cap L^{2}(|x|^{2\alpha}dx)$ under the sharp regularity assumption $s\ge a\alpha$, for $\alpha\in[1/2,5/2+a)$, where the zero mean condition is required for $\alpha\ge 3/2+a$. Finally, we prove the unique continuation principles associated with the optimal decay rates $|x|^{3/2+a}$ and $|x|^{5/2+a}$ under optimal regularity assumptions. Our approach relies on weighted energy estimates, commutator expansions for the fractional Laplacian and pseudo-differential calculus.

In this paper, we study the stability threshold of the two-dimensional incompressible MHD equations near Couette flow and a constant horizontal magnetic field \(( eta,0)\) on \(\mathbb T	imes\mathbb R\). For \(N>10\), \(0<
u,\mu\le1\) and \(| eta|\ge(
u+\mu)/(3\sqrt{
u\mu})\), we prove global stability for initial perturbations of size \(\delta_N\min\{
u,\mu\}^{1/3}\) in \(H^N\), where \(\delta_N>0\) is independent of \(
u,\mu, eta\). We also obtain enhanced dissipation of the nonzero horizontal modes on the time scale \(\min\{
u,\mu\}^{-1/3}\), together with inviscid damping of the vertical components. The proof combines time-dependent Fourier multipliers with an energy correction constructed using the Alfv'en oscillations. By combining the nonlinear terms arising from this correction, we obtain the cancellation needed to close the energy estimates at the $1/3$ scale.

In this paper we consider nonlinear biharmonic equations with $p$-Laplacian ($p\ge2$) of the form
  $$
  \left\{ \begin{array}{l}
  \Delta^2 u - \Delta_p u + V (x) u = f (x, u) \text{,}
  u \in H^2 (\mathbb{R}^N) \text{,}
  \end{array} \right.
  $$
  where the potential $V(x)$ may be indefinite. Using local linking and Morse theory, nontrivial solutions are obtained. In case the nonlinearity $f(x,\cdot)$ is odd, we obtain a sequence of large energy solutions. In the second part of the paper, for bounded positive potential, we get multiple solutions for the case that $$f(x,u)=\lambda g (x) | u |^{q - 2} u + | u |^{m
  - 2} u$$
  with exponent $m$ critical or subcritical.
